    "q-poc-off": {
      "notes": "missing: \n- node content author (model name who wrote it, thinking effort if available + user name if he edited it), this i a node metadata like the state (\"LIT\", ...) tag\n- token count as generation go (to know how many the graph cost to reach a given state)\n- side pannel need to be resizable\n- generation time i am ok to wait no a constraint here (keep the live stream as tokens arrive)\n- Exactly 3 options is too restrictive: i want to be able to dismiss one, ask for others, or add my own\n- i want a way to edit/correct a node content (to influence, orient or adjust the next one generation context), will be handy in case the model halucinate wrong/false info\n- delete or regenerate a node and a cancel while it streams => yes\n- home screen needs more work to be welcoming, allow edits, see progress ...\n- need the ability to choose/change llm model (even mid session)\n- a room setting pannel (sub menu in the global app setting)\n- a proper prompt engineer pre-prompt and an optimized context managment\n- ctrl + clic multiple node to generate a new node merging the ideas\n- settings pannel: to connect the llm provider (v0.1.0 is focused to work with a claude code subscription plan but later codex or other provider even api key suport, when implemented we will have a focus on security here (probably nex version))\nLantern is like Prism, the lantern app (will) have multiple room to do different things. Each room can have multiple spaces.\nLantern spaces example:\n- learning space (the poc)\n- welcome (landing) space to start a new subject or pick a recent one to continue a previous session (up to 3 most recent session)\n- gallery to browse the knowlege exploration with associated stats ",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-01T20:00:31.722Z"
    },
    "q-poc-keep": {
      "notes": "the color theme, subltle animation, nice detail (travelling light, ...) making a propice learning place no distraction but still appealing. this first room brighten by the learning lantern (warm light in a peacefull place) is perfect. Note: other room may use a different latern for a different feeling but the overall Lantern app need to stay coherent.\nThe tutor tone is ok but should be selectable (explain me like i am 5, engineer, ...).\nThe rhythm is great.\nStats are cool and accessible but not the main subject. Legend is mandatory.\nText highlight, \nGo bach to Lantern, the room name, the room space (to add), title, stats, ...\nReading pannel: on the right, already good (markdown rendering support is mandatory)    ",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-01T19:25:17.893Z"
    },
